# 008 · Community files and contributor docs

**Status:** `READY` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Tester basics

## What

Add SECURITY.md (through GitHub's private vulnerability reporting), CONTRIBUTING.md, a code of conduct, issue templates and a pull request template. The bug report asks for the OS, the container engine, the compose tool, the rig-check results and the logs. Rewrite AGENTS.md and CONVENTIONS.md so every rule an outside contributor needs is public. Make the contributor part of `docs/local-development.md` the contributor guide. Its operator tasks move into the docs site with goal [060](060-docs-site.goal).

## Why

Outside testers need a place to report problems and a way to send changes. Today the contributor docs send people to private files.

## Done when

- [ ] Each file exists, and GitHub shows the security policy and the templates.
- [ ] No public document tells a contributor to read a private file.
- [ ] The contributor guide is in `docs/`, and the docs index links it.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-19, owner: The community files ship with v0.1.0.

## Open questions

- The terms in them. Proposed: no contributor agreement, no sign-off rule, and the Contributor Covenant as the code of conduct.

## Progress

- 2026-10-19: Goal written from the v0.1.0 release plan.
- 2026-10-19: The operator half of `docs/local-development.md` moved to goal [060](060-docs-site.goal), the documentation site.

